Philip Allen, played by William Hurt.

10
01:19:31,428 --> 01:19:37,428
Joseph Palmi, played by Joe Pesci.

11
01:27:28,571 --> 01:27:34,571
The Good Shepherd is a 2006 American spy film produced and directed by Robert De Niro, and starring
Matt Damon, Angelina Jolie and De Niro, supported by an extensive ensemble cast.

12
01:35:25,714 --> 01:35:31,714
The film follows Edward Wilson, a fictional counterintelligence officer,
from 1939 to 1961 as the CIA develops and grows around him.

13
01:43:22,857 --> 01:43:28,857
Wilson (played by Damon), a senior CIA officer, discovers a mole in his
department following the disastrous Bay of Pigs invasion of 1961.

14
01:51:20,000 --> 01:51:26,000
The film delves into Wilson's complex life, starting from his college years at Yale in 1939, his initiation into
the Skull and Bones fraternity, and his recruitment into intelligence work (during World War II).

15
01:59:17,142 --> 01:59:23,142
His personal life is marked by a strained marriage to Margaret "Clover" Russell (played by Jolie), and by a
series of affairs, that underscore the sacrifices, and moral compromises, invited by espionage work.

16
02:07:14,285 --> 02:07:20,285
The narrative unfolds through a mix of sequential events and flashbacks, exploring the origins of the CIA, the Wilson character's
involvement in key historical events, and the personal tolls typical in careers dedicated to secret intelligence.

17
02:15:11,428 --> 02:15:17,428
The film was released on December 22, 2006 by Universal Pictures in North America and by
Morgan Creek International in international markets, to mixed reviews.

18
02:23:08,571 --> 02:23:14,571
It grossed $100 million against an estimated $80 million production budget.

19
02:31:05,714 --> 02:31:11,714
The film explores themes of berlin, germany, london, england, central
intelligence agency (cia), husband wife relationship, cuba.

20
02:39:02,857 --> 02:39:08,857
The tone is emotional and intense.
